l information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Sustainable Research Officer Job id: 160445. Salary: £39,076 - £43,909 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 12 October 2026. Closing date: 01 November 2026. Business unit: Research Platforms. Department: Research Platforms Office. Contact details: Marcelo Salierno.  marcelo.salierno@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us The Sustainability in Research Team works with research and technical communities across King’s to reduce the environmental impact of research. We support laboratories, research facilities and digital research teams to use resources, equipment, energy and data more sustainably. Our work supports King’s sustainability targets, UKRI Concordat priorities and emerging sustainability requirements for research funding. Following 100% LEAF accreditation in 2025, we’re continuing to help laboratories strengthen their sustainable practices and work towards the highest level of accreditation by 2030. We also support sustainable computing, waste and resource management, and practical initiatives that help embed sustainability across our research environments. About the role We’re looking for a Sustainable Research Officer to help research teams improve the sustainability of their day-to-day work. Reporting to the Sustainable Research & Innovation Lead, you’ll work closely with laboratory sustainability leads, technical staff, researchers and professional services colleagues across King’s. A key part of the role will be: Drive Sustainability Accreditations: Guide wet and dry laboratories through sustainable research frameworks, including LEAF, Green Disc, SparkHub, and MyGreenLab. Deliver Practical Guidance: Empower laboratory teams to adopt sustainable daily practices and co-facilitate interactive workshops. Advance Sustainable Computing: Collaborate with the e-Research team to help computational researchers optimise data management and computing workflows for lower environmental impact. You’ll coordinate sustainability projects and be involved in our campaigns, including energy-saving activities, supplier take-back schemes and waste minimisation programmes. You’ll work with laboratory teams to increase participation and support safe, compliant and sustainable waste practices. The role will also involve coordinating activities, collecting and reporting data and creating clear, engaging communications and guidance. This is a varied and collaborative role for someone who can turn sustainability goals into practical improvements across laboratory and research environments. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week) offered on an indefinite contract. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria 1.      Experience supporting or implementing laboratory sustainability initiatives and projects that promote sustainable research practices and operational improvements with in a lab environment. 2.      Knowledge of, and experience supporting accreditation processes for the Laboratory Efficiency Assessment Framework (LEAF). 3.      Understanding of sustainable waste management practices and environmental compliance requirements, including the ability to interpret and apply relevant policies and standards. 4.      Experience organising or delivering training, workshops or engagement activities for diverse audiences. 5.      Strong project coordination and administrative skills, with the ability to manage multiple activities and meet competing deadlines. 6.      Experience collecting, analysing and presenting data to monitor performance, identify improvement opportunities and support decision-making. 7.      Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience producing guidance, training materials, digital content or other engagement resources for students and research lab staff. 8.      Ability to build effective working relationships and engage a wide range of stakeholders, including researchers, technical staff, professional services colleagues and external suppliers. Desirable criteria 1.      Familiarity with Green DiSC and sustainable data management practices. 2.       Knowledge of best practices in laboratory sustainability. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Sustainable Research Officer | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160445-sustainable-research-officer Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link o