escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 160305 . Salary: :  £39,076 – 43,909 inclusive of £5,125 London weighting allowance . Posted: 13 October 2026 . Closing date: 28 October 2026 . Business unit: Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine . Department: St John's Institute of Dermatology . Contact details: Kingsley Powell . kingsley.powell@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Hospital . Category: No category added . Back to job search About us St John’s Institute of Dermatology provides a range of services and facilities to support research aimed at improving outcomes in people with skin disease including skin inflammation, skin cancer and rare skin disease. Work extends from genetic discovery through to a comprehensive portfolio of clinical trials (phase II onwards) and biomarker-enabled precision medicine. The Unit works with investigators within both the academic and industry community. About the role This role is a fantastic opportunity to work in a fast-paced environment in an internationally renowned dermatology research centre, host to major programmes of work related to skin inflammation, cancer and rare skin diseases that aim to understand why disease develops and then how and when to intervene. The post-holder will support a varied portfolio of research that delivers novel interventions, digital transformation, and personalised medicine in severe skin diseases, including eczema and psoriasis. They will be allocated specific studies within this portfolio, and work closely with the Programme Manager to ensure these studies are delivered according to milestones. They will co-ordinate the design, implementation and running of clinical studies across participating sites, as well as supporting the dissemination of research findings. The post-holder will join a friendly and high-achieving team of clinical and translational researchers, statisticians, laboratory technicians, trial managers, and data managers to deliver impactful research. The role would suit a motivated and proactive individual with a firm grounding and interest in collaborative clinical research. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week) based on-site, and you will be offered an a fixed term contract until 31/03/2028. Research staff at King’s are entitled to at least 10 days per year (pro-rata) for professional development. This entitlement, from the Concordat to Support the Career Development of Researchers , applies to Postdocs, Research Assistants, Research and Teaching Technicians, Teaching Fellows and AEP equivalent up to and including grade 7. Visit the Centre for Research Staff Development for more information. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Good first degree and masters in a relevant subject Excellent project management skills and teamwork with a ‘can do’ attitude and approach Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills, with experience of multi-stakeholder engagement Strong IT skills, including working knowledge of Microsoft Office and databases Ability to work without direct supervision; to manage own workload through and display good organisational ability Excellent knowledge of the key frameworks, standards, principles and regulations that govern UK research including Good Clinical Practice, Data Protection Act and the UK Policy Framework for Health and Social Care Research Experience in the development of key research related materials, such as protocols, operation manuals, standard operating procedures and guidance documents, or with demonstrated evidence of similar experience within a relevant area Desirable criteria Clinical Trial/Study Management Experience Experience using social media to promote science and/or direct to patient recruitment strategies Experience of report/paper writing Experience of budget management Experience of industry/capital/research liaising Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information We pride ourselves on being inclusive and welcoming. We embrace diversity and want everyone to feel that they belong and are connected to others in our community. We are committed to working with our staff and unions on these and other issues, to continue to support our people and to develop a diverse and inclusive culture at King's. As part of this commitment to equality, diversity and inclusion and through this appointment process, it is our aim to develop candidate pools that include applicants from all backgrounds and communities. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit ’ pages. This post is subject to Disclosure and Barring Service and Occupational Health clearances. Apply now Apply now Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link"
