nities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link IT Officer Job id: 160485. Salary: £34,713 - £38,127 per annum, inclusive of London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 14 October 2026. Closing date: 01 November 2026. Business unit: Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine. Department: Analytics, Environmental & Forensics. Contact details: Jayla Mehmet.  Jayla.mehmetkcl.ac.uk Location: Waterloo Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About Us The DCC is the only World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA) accredited laboratory in the UK and is therefore an important sovereign facility.  It played a key role in the London 2012 Olympics, Glasgow 2022 Commonwealth Games and 2021 Rugby League World Cup sports testing programmes as well as the UEFA Men’s and Women’s Football Tournaments (the EUROs) and most recently the European Athletics Championships (2026). The DCC is also accredited by the UK Accreditation Service (UKAS) as a testing laboratory, in accordance with IEC/ISO 17025. The post holder will therefore need a meticulous approach to work and understand the importance of maintaining quality standards within a highly structured laboratory unit. To contribute to the development and implementation of the Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS) for the Drug Control Centre in order to maintain accreditation to ISO 17025 and World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA) International Standard for Laboratories. The Post holder will be a member of the DCCs IT team, providing high quality expertise in IT and data handling implemented through the Laboratory Information Management Systems (LIMS) under the direction of the Senior IT officer.  This role is campus-based because of the nature of the data handled, confidentiality and security are paramount for data integrity. About The Role The post holder will be knowledgeable and competent in the use of standard software packages (Excel, Access or Power-BI) and be able to integrate and evaluation complex data. The post-holder will contribute to the delivery of a bespoke IT service across the Drug Control Centre. This involves supporting the Senior IT Officer to ensure the efficient, secure functioning of the test result and other analytical data created through the analysis of biological samples in accordance with the World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA) Code’s International Standard for Laboratories and World Anti-Doping Agency and ISO 17025 accreditations. Part of the role will be to develop proven LIMS expertise and authoritative knowledge to data processes and procedures with respect to IT Systems.  This will include delivering the individual sample number project under the supervision of the Senior IT officer to ensure the integrity of LIMS throughout the sample journey (booking in, communicating data to analytical instruments, analysts and customers) including reporting, data backup and archiving) . The post holder will work to maintain full compliance with title 21 of the CFR part 11 (Code of Federal Regulations) that defines the criteria under which electronic records and electronic signatures are considered trustworthy, reliable, and equivalent to paper records. Under the direction of the Senior IT Officer the post holder will develop knowledge and expert understanding of the use of Power-BI for the dissemination of management information: provide Key Performance Indicator for members of the senior team. They will support the Senior IT Officer to integrate laboratory processes within the LIMS system towards a paper-less service for anti-doping, clinical and forensics samples. This may include supporting the Senior IT Officer to integrate machine learning initiatives into the DCC to ensure the continuous improvement of the LIMS Systems (e.g., for invoicing and management reports). Routine tasks will include monitoring compliance against applicable standards and regulations providing a quarterly report on common issues to the Quality & Health and Safety meetings; implementation of the review and validation of DCC spreadsheets and the WADA spreadsheets for threshold substances and the IT software and hardware Inventory maintained as an electronic record. The post holder is expected to actively engage in Continuing Professional Development and training initiatives. This is a full-time on-campus post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an indefinite contract. About You To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Experience of working in a relevant/similar post Good (moderate to advanced) Microsoft Office app skills, with experience of using, maintaining and analysing large and complex datasets Knowledge of machine learning and AI approaches Evidence of working with electronic records and electronic signatures using standard operating procedures to produce trustworthy, reliable secure documentation Experience of large data handling and evaluation Experience of collating information with emphasis on data integrity /confidentiality into report format ability to present complex information clearly Knowledge and experience of developing databases in Microsoft Access or other comparable software packages Desirable criteria Experience working with and developing a LIMS system. Experience of working in a highly regulated context or an accredited Laboratory, and being familiar with document/version control in line with regulatory requirements Working knowledge of Microsoft Power BI Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box IT Officer | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160485-it-officer Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
